KG42.register("rules-2c69deedf6b79a5d515f5433",{"id":"12-p2p_microgrid_trading::v141-c-R005","paper":"12-p2p_microgrid_trading","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R005","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Market payment","process_stage":"settlement","market_meaning":"Energy exchange precedes the final settlement of bills and transactions through payment. Scope: The stated P2P energy-trading process sequence. The difference between promised and actual electricity generation or consumption must be calculated and charged during settlement. Scope: Settlement of differences between promised and actual P2P electricity generation or consumption. Condition: Promised and actual electricity generation or consumption quantities differ.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function settlement.payment under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["execution.energy_trade","settlement.payment"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R005-E001","source":"execution.energy_trade","target":"settlement.payment","type":"precedes","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R005-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-10"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Settlement of differences between promised and actual P2P electricity generation or consumption. | The stated P2P energy-trading process sequence.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-10","v141-b-g01-ev-11"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Energy exchange precedes the final settlement of bills and transactions through payment. Scope: The stated P2P energy-trading process sequence.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["execution.energy_trade","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-10"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The difference between promised and actual electricity generation or consumption must be calculated and charged during settlement. Scope: Settlement of differences between promised and actual P2P electricity generation or consumption. Condition: Promised and actual electricity generation or consumption quantities differ.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-11"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-10","location":{"location_id":"src-c1934be9b4-p03-c1r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"2. Four-layer system architecture of Peer-to-Peer energy trading","anchor_text":"g , p coordinated way either connected to the main power network or is- ti landed. A Microgrid norma","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 1","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The third dimension shows the time sequence of the P2P energy trading process. Bidding is the first process of P2P energy trading when energy customers (generators, consumers and prosumers) reach trading agreements with each other prior to the energy exchange. During the bidding process, energy customers interact with each other and agree on the price and amount of energy to be traded. Energy exchanging is the second process, during which energy is generated, transmitted and consumed. Settlement is the final process when bills and transactions are finally settled via settlement arrangements and payment."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-11","location":{"location_id":"src-c1934be9b4-p03-c1r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"2. Four-layer system architecture of Peer-to-Peer energy trading","anchor_text":"the second process, during which energy is generated, transmitted and en consumed. Settlement is the","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Considering the physical network constraints and uncertainty of DERs, a seller who has promised to sell a certain amount of electricity sometimes is unable to generate that exact amount as listed in the orders. The similar situation also applies to a buyer. The difference between the promised and actual electricity generation or consumption quantity needs to be calculated and charged during the settlement."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":"The rule evidence describes a process sequence and a settlement-time charging obligation, not an optimization problem with decision variables. The source text attached to this rule does not define symbol names, domains, or units for promised electricity, actual electricity, or any settlement decision, and the frozen graph has no data/quantity nodes to bind such variables. Adding x objects such as q_promised or q_actual would invent symbols and roles beyond the supplied evidence.","empty_theta_reason":"The rule evidence attaches no fixed parameters, constants, coefficients, prices, or penalty values for payment or for the promised-versus-actual difference. The quantities referred to in v141-b-g01-ev-11 are described as promised and actual amounts, not as given constants in this rule's evidence. Adding theta objects would invent parameter values or definitions not present in the supplied source text for this rule."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-participation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"settlement.payment","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-10","quote":"Energy exchanging is the second process, during which energy is generated, transmitted and consumed. Settlement is the final process when bills and transactions are finally settled via settlement arrangements and payment."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-11","quote":"The difference between the promised and actual electricity generation or consumption quantity needs to be calculated and charged during the settlement."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"f19343ab5364fd16164e964f2c1cdbc80a6ff0c0ad656448293e74360a7596ff","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"The frozen rule is a procedural settlement rule. Its two constraints state a stage precedence (energy exchange precedes settlement/payment) and an obligation to calculate and charge a promised-versus-actual electricity difference during settlement. The rule evidence v141-b-g01-ev-10 and v141-b-g01-ev-11 supply no equation, symbol definitions, domains, units, coefficients, or parameter values for the promised quantity, actual quantity, difference, or charge. The existing C.1 constraints are therefore retained as not_formalized with expression=null. This is not a determination that the source lacks related settlement mathematics elsewhere; it records that this rule's frozen graph and attached evidence do not contain a supported mathematical expression. B evidence remains unreviewed per the experiment, and no source correctness is claimed.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R005-C001","node_ids":["execution.energy_trade","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R005-E001"],"rationale":"Graph-membership binding only, not a mathematical formalization. C001 states that energy exchange precedes final settlement/payment, which is exactly the frozen precedence edge v141-c-R005-E001 from execution.energy_trade to settlement.payment. No expression is asserted because the evidence provides only procedural ordering."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R005-C002","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Graph-membership binding only, not a mathematical formalization. C002 concerns the settlement-stage obligation triggered by a difference between promised and actual electricity generation or consumption, so its only frozen node in scope is settlement.payment. The rule graph contains no edge or quantity node representing the discrepancy calculation or charge, and the evidence supplies no symbols or formula to invent one."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
